        {
          "page": 6,
          "section": "2.2. Materials and characterization",
          "quote": "The selected alloy W10 Mo 27 Cr 21 Ti 22 Al 20 was prepared by vacuum arc melting (VAM). High purity molten Ti was used as a getter for residual oxygen, nitrogen and hydrogen in the high vacuum chamber. All five powdered elements with a purity of over 99.5% were compacted in the form of pellets. At first, the pellets of elements Al, Ti and Cr were melted and the ingot of these elements was obtained. Then the ingot of W and Mo was obtained similarly and added to first ingot. Finally, both ingots were remelted four times to ensure the homogeneity of the alloy.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "72ab510a0076d6a5:part:001"
        }
      ]
    }
